{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779504102,"nonce":"oJH9co1454Io5R/F0uS66ni1ibQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0DMw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/165","origin":"github"},"title":"Hover convergence shows pre-convergence drift — cross-event analysis needed","message":"## Symptom\n\nDuring [#160](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160) (2026-05-22 deployment), **multiple hover engagements showed pre-convergence drift** — the boat drifted noticeably before finally heading to the hover location. Most clearly observed at end of a 2-line survey: transition to HOVER, then visible drift before convergence.\n\nMultiple hover events across the deployment (after mooring extraction, between survey loops, manual-mode → drift-test transition, end-of-mission) provide a multi-sample dataset for analysis.\n\n## Investigation scope (operator-requested)\n\nPer dev log (line 188, paraphrased): \"inspect every hover engagement across the deployment, not just the one drifty-hover at end-of-2-line-survey.\"\n\nCross-event analysis lets us disambiguate three candidate causes:\n\n1. **Battery-state effects** — thruster authority drops at low SOC; hover convergence may degrade gracefully with voltage. If drift magnitude correlates with battery voltage, this is the dominant cause.\n2. **Controller tuning** — hover controller gains may be tuned for a different operating point (higher voltage, different wind/current). If drift is uniform across battery state but varies with wind/current, this is the cause.\n3. **State-machine transition** — the transition into HOVER may have a built-in deadband or initialization step that produces consistent pre-convergence drift regardless of conditions.\n\n## Diagnosis (post-processing)\n\nBag analysis from #160 in-water bag(s):\n\nFor each hover event:\n- Timestamp of transition-into-hover (state-machine change)\n- Boat position vs. hover-target position over the first ~30 s post-transition\n- Battery voltage at transition (loaded reading)\n- Wind/current at transition (if available from logged sensors)\n- `cmd_vel` profile during convergence\n- Convergence time (time-to-within-X-meters of target)\n\nBuild a table indexed by hover event; look for the pattern.\n\n## Class-prep impact\n\nFor Summer Hydro 2026, the survey workflow uses HOVER between line transitions. Pre-convergence drift extends mission time per line transition and can place the boat in less predictable positions during student observation. Severity depends on whether the drift is order-of-magnitude consistent (workable) or randomized (potentially confusing for students).\n\nPriority: medium. Not class-blocking but a class-quality concern.\n\n## Context\n\n- Originating deployment: #160 (2026-05-22)\n- Dev log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_dev_logs.md` — \"transitioned to HOVER, but drifted noticeably\" + \"inspect every hover engagement\" entries\n- Bags: see #160 wrap-up for paths\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}